# Example integration point only. This is not an active Apache configuration.
#
# Generate the real fragment from a reviewed, non-secret manifest:
#   node scripts/entreprises/render-company-proxy.mjs --input companies.json \
#     --output infra/atelier/apache/cerp-business-companies.include.conf
#
# Put the generated Include before the existing legacy ProxyPass /api/ and
# ProxyPass /socket.io/ catch-alls in cerp-local.conf / the WireGuard boundary.
# It routes only registered company+database pairs to fixed targets. It does not
# replace backend JWT/company authorization and must never be used as a dynamic
# proxy template. The VPS public proxy must preserve both headers and the full
# Socket.IO query string to this Apache boundary.
#
# IncludeOptional /etc/apache2/conf-available/cerp-business-companies.include.conf
